{
  "$comment": [
    "Shared interest fixture — the contract between two implementations.",
    "",
    "Asserted by apps/api (Jest) and apps/mobile (Dart). Both must produce these",
    "numbers exactly. The server value is authoritative; the client computes the",
    "same figure so an offline user sees the right number before syncing.",
    "",
    "Every expectation here was verified by hand, not generated from either",
    "implementation — a fixture derived from the code it checks proves only that",
    "the code equals itself.",
    "",
    "amounts are paise; rateBp is basis points PER PERIOD (2% monthly = 200)."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "simple-1-month",
      "why": "₹5,000 at 2% per month for exactly one month is ₹100.",
      "principalPaise": 500000,
      "rateBp": 200,
      "type": "simple",
      "frequency": "monthly",
      "fromDate": "2026-01-01",
      "asOf": "2026-01-31",
      "days": 30,
      "expectedInterestPaise": 10000
    },
